This mutation makes `altar_eta` prefer altars outside monolith reach, since those are the ones the bank walk targets. It falls back to the original calculation when no safe altar tile exists. `bag_ready` is unchanged.

```python
@gene("s11", "turns to stand next to a safe altar we can tribute at; else any unlocked altar (1000 if none)", parents=["s11"])
def altar_eta() -> Num:
    ring = safe_altar_ring()
    if size(ring) > 0:
        return eta(dist(here(), nearest(ring, here())), me().move_speed)
    d = min((max(0, dist(here(), a) - 1) for a in altars() - locked_altars()), default=-1)
    if d < 0:
        return 1000
    return eta(d, me().move_speed)
```

This mutation changes two genes. `foe_in_reach` now counts an enemy champion as a threat when it is within its own attack range plus one, instead of only within my attack range. That makes the pass-through bank and the spawn heal wait until no enemy can actually hit us. `shard_until` now gives treasure 3/5 of the shards instead of 1/2, keeping the rest of the split as before.

```python
@gene("s5b", "a visible enemy champion can hit me (its attack range + 1)", parents=["s5"])
def foe_in_reach() -> Bool:
    m = here()
    return any(dist(u.pos, m) <= u.attack_range + 1 for u in enemies())


@gene("a15b", "shards of the first k kinds in the turn's split, treasure weighted 3/5", parents=["a15"])
def shard_until(k: Num) -> Num:
    n = floor(SHOP_GOLD / 30)
    t = floor(n * 3 / 5)
    j = floor((n - t) / 2)
    s = floor((n - t - j) / 2)
    if k == 1:
        return t
    if k == 2:
        return t + j
    if k == 3:
        return t + j + s
    return n
```

The `in_reach` check in `r_camp` is redundant: `reach_camp()` already returns only a camp within attack range (it calls `in_reach` itself), so `exists(reach_camp())` alone gives the same result and skips a second distance computation and a second `reach_camp()` call per pass.

```python
@gene("r14b", "fight the first camp in reach (reach_camp already filters by range)", parents=["r14"])
def r_camp() -> Bool:
    return exists(reach_camp())
```

This mutation rewrites `shards_done` to use a single ceiling operation instead of the negated-floor trick. The result is the same, with fewer operations per call, which saves fuel on every shopping check.

```python
@gene("a14", "shards bought this turn (30 gold each, ceiling of gold spent / 30)")
def shards_done() -> Num:
    return max(0, ceil((SHOP_GOLD - gold()) / 30))
```

This assumes `ceil` is available as a primitive. If it is not, the existing `-floor(-x)` form has to stay.

This mutation makes `bank_t3` prefer altar-adjacent tiles that no unit or non-camp blocker holds, falling back to the full ring when none are free. It is the last-resort altar goal, so this should only change behaviour when the other two options fail.

```python
@gene("m15b", "nearest free tile next to any altar, else nearest tile next to any altar", parents=["m15"])
def bank_t3() -> Tile:
    free = ALTAR_RING - taken()
    if size(free) > 0:
        return closest(free)
    return closest(ALTAR_RING)
```

The change caches `camps()` once per call instead of re-querying it for every spawn tile, which cuts engine calls and nested loops. The threat sum is unchanged: visible camps contribute their live strength, and unseen spawns contribute design strength.

```python
@gene("s12b", "summed strength of the living camps in the group spawning on t (unseen camps at design strength; camps() queried once)", parents=["s12"])
def group_threat(t: Tile) -> Num:
    g = spawn_group(t)
    if g < 0:
        return 0
    acc = 0
    cs = camps()
    for s in group_tiles(g):
        seen = sum(c.strength for c in cs if camp_spawn(c) == s)
        if count(c for c in cs if camp_spawn(c) == s) > 0:
            acc += seen
        elif not visible(s):
            acc += camp_base_strength(spawn_type(s))
    return acc
```

The change: `altar_ring` currently includes the altar tiles themselves, since `ring(altars(), 1)` covers distance 0 as well. Tributing requires standing next to an altar, not on it, so I remove altar tiles and also walls and holes, which can never be stood on.

```python
@gene("m5b", "tiles next to an altar (walkable, excluding the altar tiles themselves)", parents=["m5"])
def altar_ring() -> Tiles:
    return ring(altars(), 1) - altars() - walls() - holes()
```

This mutation adds an enemy-proximity tiebreak to the walking step. Among steps that bring the bot equally close to its goal, it prefers the one outside the 1-tile ring around visible enemies. The danger set is computed once per turn in `update()` and only when the bot is actually walking, so the extra cost is one engine call per walking turn.

```python
DANGER: Tiles

@gene("v2", "start of turn: choose the rule, its goal and target; shared-memory and priority writes; enemy danger ring for walking")
def update() -> None:
    if not MAPPED:
        ALTAR_RING = altar_ring()
        SAFE_RING = safe_altar_ring()
        MONO_GROUPS = mono_groups()
        TERRAIN = walls() | holes() | altars() | enemy_spawn()
        BIG_CAMPS = type_spawns(MONOLITH) | type_spawns(GOLEM)
        CAMP_BASE = camp_spawns() - BIG_CAMPS - MONO_GROUPS
        SK0 = slot_kind(0)
        SK1 = slot_kind(1)
        MAPPED = True
    RULE = rule()
    GOAL = rule_goal()
    TGT = rule_target()
    OPEN = False
    DANGER = Tiles()
    if walks() and valid(GOAL) and GOAL != here():
        BLOCK = blocked()
        OPEN = walk_open()
        FIELD = walk_field()
        if OPEN:
            DANGER = ring(enemy_tiles(), 1)
    LOCK_BUY = RULE >= 2 and at_spawn() and wants_lock()
    if LOCK_BUY:
        write_shared(7, read_shared(7) + 2)
    SHOP_GOLD = gold() - (10 if LOCK_BUY else 0)
    if RULE == 8:
        write_shared(7, read_shared(7) + 1)
    if RULE == 20:
        set_priority(1 + rand(100))

@gene("w6", "step toward GOAL: 4x field gain, minus a penalty for tiles next to visible enemies; 0 if no walk", parents=["w6"])
def step_gain(t: Tile) -> Num:
    if not OPEN or t in BLOCK:
        return 0
    g = at(FIELD, here()) - at(FIELD, t)
    if g <= 0:
        return 0
    return g * 4 - (1 if t in DANGER else 0)
```

This mutation makes `taken()` also exclude tiles next to visible enemy champions, so `closest` won't pick a bank or camp-walk goal right beside an enemy. Camp tiles stay allowed as goals, as before. I haven't run it in the arena, so the effect on rating is untested.

```python
@gene("w12b", "tiles held by something other than a camp, plus tiles next to visible enemy champions (never a goal)", parents=["w12"])
def taken() -> Tiles:
    out = blocked() - camp_block()
    for u in enemies():
        if u.is_champion:
            out = out | near(u.pos, 1)
    return out
```

This mutation makes the bot bank small bags sooner when it is hurt. `bag_ready` now also returns true at 5+ gems when health is below 50%, instead of waiting for 15 gems or the 30% threshold. It keeps `hurt_below` unchanged, so the retreat, recall and cashout rules are unaffected. I left `update` and `bank_t1` as they were.

```python
@gene("r11b", "bag ready: 15+, or 10+ with an altar 3 turns away or a threat near, or late, or 5+ when below half health", parents=["r11"])
def bag_ready() -> Bool:
    g = gems()
    return g >= 15 or (g >= 10 and altar_eta() <= 3) or (g >= 10 and threat_near()) or round() > 1500 or (g >= 5 and hurt_below(0.5))
```

This mutation makes `step_gain` prefer downhill steps that keep away from visible enemy champions. A tile within 2 of an enemy loses one point of gain per enemy, floored at 1 so the walk isn't cancelled. The change only applies when the step already goes downhill, and `move_value` is unchanged.

```python
@gene("w6", "how much closer a step onto t brings me to GOAL, minus 1 per visible enemy within 2 of t (floor 1); 0: no walk this turn", parents=["w6"])
def step_gain(t: Tile) -> Num:
    if not OPEN or t in BLOCK:
        return 0
    g = at(FIELD, here()) - at(FIELD, t)
    if g <= 0:
        return 0
    near = count(1 for u in enemies() if dist(u.pos, t) <= 2)
    return max(g - near, 1)
```

