The change makes `fight_foe` skip enemies standing on their own spawn, so the bot picks the weakest attackable champion that is not camping spawn, instead of locking onto a spawn-camper and then failing `r_fight`'s spawn check.

```python
@gene("s13", "the weakest enemy champion in reach, skipping any standing on its own spawn")
def fight_foe() -> Unit:
    return best(enemies(), lambda u: -u.health if (in_reach(u) and not (u.pos in enemy_spawn())) else -INF)
```

```python
@gene("r7", "fight the weakest enemy champion in reach (not on its own spawn)", parents=["r7"])
def r_fight() -> Bool:
    f = fight_foe()
    return exists(f) and dist(here(), f.pos) <= me().attack_range and not (f.pos in enemy_spawn())
```

This mutation changes `bank_t3` so it prefers altar-adjacent tiles that are camp spawns. That makes `bank_blocked` fire when a blocked altar's ring includes a camp spawn, instead of requiring the nearest ring tile to be one. `bank_goal` also calls `bank_t3`, so its fallback will prefer blocking camp spawns too.

